---
description: TypeScript standards for all frontend applications.
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeScript Standards

Strict mode is mandatory.

Never disable strict mode.

---

# any

Never use:

any

unless absolutely unavoidable.

Prefer:

unknown

or

Generics.

---

# Type vs Interface

Use:

interface

for object contracts.

Use:

type

for unions,

mapped types,

utility types,

aliases.

---

# Enums

Avoid enums.

Prefer:

const objects

or

union types.

---

# Nullability

Never assume values exist.

Always handle:

null

undefined

optional values.

---

# Assertions

Avoid:

as

unless fully justified.

Prefer proper type inference.

---

# Generics

Use generics when reusable.

Avoid overengineering.

---

# Props

Always define explicit Props interfaces.

Never inline complex prop types.

---

# Utility Types

Prefer built-in utilities:

Partial

Required

Pick

Omit

Record

Readonly

Awaited

ReturnType

Parameters

---

# Imports

Prefer type imports.

Example

import type { User }

---

# API Models

Separate:

DTO

API Response

Database Entity

UI Model

Never mix them.

---

# Validation

Runtime validation belongs to Zod.

TypeScript is compile-time only.

---

# Goal

Every line should be type-safe.